part.text:
**CONFIRMED**: In Spring Security 6.x, `@EnableWebSecurity` is NO LONGER meta-annotated with `@Configuration`! (In 5.x it was; in 6.0 they removed it — @EnableWebSecurity only has @Retention, @Target, @Documented, @Import(WebSecurityConfiguration, SpringWebMvcImportSelector, OAuth2ImportSelector, HttpSecurityConfiguration), @EnableGlobalAuthentication.)

So in Spring Security 6, a class annotated only with @EnableWebSecurity (no @Configuration) is treated as a **lite** configuration? Hmm — no: without @Configuration, the class is still picked up by component scanning IF it has... wait — component scan picks up @Component-derived stereotypes. @EnableWebSecurity is not a @Component stereotype → **the class isn't detected by scanning at all**?? Hmm — no wait — Spring's component scanning (ClassPathScanningCandidateComponentProvider) includes classes annotated with @Configuration OR any @Component-derived OR... hmm — actually, in Spring Framework 6, `AnnotationConfigUtils` — the scan filters on @Component-stereotypes. @EnableWebSecurity is NOT a stereotype. BUT — hold on — in the ORIGINAL (Spring Security 5.7), @EnableWebSecurity WAS meta-annotated @Configuration → and @Configuration IS a @Component stereotype (via @Component meta-annotation on @Configuration? @Configuration is meta-annotated with @Component? Hmm — actually @Configuration is itself annotated with @Component in Spring? No! @Configuration is NOT @Component-annotated... wait — hmm. Let me think: Spring's @Configuration:

```java
@Target(ElementType.TYPE)
@Retention(RetentionPolicy.RUNTIME)
@Documented
@Component
public @interface Configuration {
```

YES — @Configuration is meta-annotated with @Component in Spring Framework (since 3.x? Hmm — hmm, actually I recall @Configuration having @Component since... yes, in Spring 4.3+? Hmm — it's been @Component for a long time). So in Security 5.x, @EnableWebSecurity (meta @Configuration meta @Component) made SecurityConfiguration eligible for component scanning.

In Security 6.0, @EnableWebSecurity LOST the @Configuration meta-annotation → classes annotated ONLY with @EnableWebSecurity are NOT picked up by component scanning → the SecurityConfiguration bean is never registered → passwordEncoder @Bean missing → UserService fails!! THAT'S THE BUG. And also the security filter chain is missing entirely!

**FIX: add `@Configuration` to SecurityConfiguration.** This is exactly what the Spring Security 6 migration guide says: "SecurityConfiguration should be annotated with @Configuration when using @EnableWebSecurity" — JHipster 8's SecurityConfiguration has @Configuration. Let me add it.

